data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2709,"item_id":"fc_0ab345649bc6d74b016adb20de6a6481919d3a3c05ba45eacb","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"For every nonnegative integer n and every nonempty compact E⊆ℝ^n, with I=[0,1] and E×I given the concatenated Euclidean metric, prove dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"nonnegative integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"subset of Euclidean ℝ^n\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-9\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-9\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"case_elimination\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\",\\\"direct\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"natural_induction\\\",\\\"negation_introduction\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Squared concatenated product distance equals the sum of squared factor distances. Projections are 1-Lipschitz; product diameters satisfy diam(U×J)≤√(diam(U)^2+diam(J)^2). Interval subdivision at scale r uses at most 1/r+1 intervals of length ≤r.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"ℝ^n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space of dimension n\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The n-dimensional Euclidean space including ℝ^0, a singleton.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"dim_H\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Hausdorff dimension\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Critical exponent of Hausdorff measures, with dim_H(∅)=0.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"I\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"subset of ℝ\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"[0,1].\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"If d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"If d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"A is a set in a Borel extended metric space; d:NNReal.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M001-0006/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"55313e0fb359726f773fe001aa619855264b1d97dbf48806a0fe170a60cd1b3b\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH.{u_1} : ∀ {X : Type u_1} [inst : EMetricSpace.{u_1} X] [inst_1 : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} X]\\\\n  [inst_2 :\\\\n    @BorelSpace.{u_1} X\\\\n      (@UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace.{u_1} X\\\\n        (@PseudoEMetricSpace.toUniformSpace.{u_1} X (@EMetricSpace.toPseudoEMetricSpace.{u_1} X inst)))\\\\n      inst_1]\\\\n  {s : Set.{u_1} X} {d : NNReal},\\\\n  @LT.lt.{0} ENNReal (@Preorder.toLT.{0} ENNReal (@PartialOrder.toPreorder.{0} ENNReal ENNReal.instPartialOrder)) (↑d)\\\\n      (@dimH.{u_1} X inst s) →\\\\n    @Eq.{1} ENNReal\\\\n      (@DFunLike.coe.{u_1 + 1, u_1 + 1, 1} (@MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} X inst_1) (Set.{u_1} X) (fun x => ENNReal)\\\\n        (@MeasureTheory.Measure.instFunLike.{u_1} X inst_1)\\\\n        (@MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure.{u_1} X inst inst_2 ↑d) s)\\\\n      (@Top.top.{0} ENNReal ENNReal.instTop)\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a countable family of nonnegative measurable ENNReal functions, the integral of their sum equals the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a countable family of nonnegative measurable ENNReal functions, the integral of their sum equals the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"Measurable space and measure; countable index set; each summand AEMeasurable.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M002-0008/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"254ede729428097ad087ac8d9763fdd9e9a429feaa566f7146c5293161f70d46\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue.Add\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"14da3dd3c269221e9ec43e91c6b22bb02d5db7f00e03c789661c72dffecf7b4a\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum.{u_1,\\\\n    u_2} : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {m : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {μ : @MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α m}\\\\n  [Countable.{u_2 + 1} β] {f : β → α → ENNReal},\\\\n  (∀ (i : β), @AEMeasurable.{u_1, 0} α ENNReal ENNReal.measurableSpace m (f i) μ) →\\\\n    @Eq.{1} ENNReal\\\\n      (@MeasureTheory.lintegral.{u_1} α m μ fun a =>\\\\n        @tsum.{0, u_2} ENNReal β ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace (fun i => f i a)\\\\n          (SummationFilter.unconditional.{u_2} β))\\\\n      (@tsum.{0, u_2} ENNReal β ENNReal.instAddCommMonoid ENNReal.instTopologicalSpace\\\\n        (fun i => @MeasureTheory.lintegral.{u_1} α m μ fun a => f i a) (SummationFilter.unconditional.{u_2} β))\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"dim_H\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Put D=dim_H(E), F=E×I. E is bounded by compactness, and finite-dimensional cube covers show D≤n. For q>D, the defining dimension threshold gives H^q(E)=0. At scale δ≤1 choose a cover with positive diameters r_j≤δ and arbitrarily small Σr_j^q; replace zero-diameter members by tiny balls with arbitrarily small added cost. Cover I above each member by ≤1/r_j+1 intervals of length ≤r_j. The product cover has diameters ≤√2r_j and total (q+1)-cost ≤2(√2)^(q+1)Σr_j^q; hence H^(q+1)(F)=0 and dim_H(F)≤D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"q\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"r_j\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D>0 take 0<s<D. M001 gives H^s(E)=∞, so contents c_s(E,δ)→∞ as δ↓0 by the defining Hausdorff-content limit. For any cover V_i of F with ρ_i=diam(V_i)≤δ≤1, project to A_i,B_i; diameters are ≤ρ_i. Enclose B_i in open J_i of length ≤ρ_i+η_i, choosing η_i>0 so Ση_iρ_i^s<ε. For every t∈I, A_i for t∈J_i cover E, because (x,t) belongs to some V_i and B_i⊆J_i. Thus c_s(E,δ)≤Σ1_{J_i}(t)ρ_i^s pointwise. Integrate: indicators are measurable; M002 gives integral of sum as sum of integrals. Therefore c_s(E,δ)≤Σ|J_i∩I|ρ_i^s≤Σρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Zero-diameter terms vanish since s>0. Let ε→0 and infimize to get c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ), hence H^(s+1)(F)=∞ and dim_H(F)≥s+1. Let s↑D.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"s\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"V_i\\\",\\\"ρ_i\\\",\\\"A_i\\\",\\\"B_i\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"η_i\\\",\\\"ε\\\",\\\"c_s\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D=0, choose x₀∈E by H001. The projection F→I is onto and 1-Lipschitz. Covering sets map to sets of no larger diameter, so dimension of an image is at most the dimension of its domain by the Hausdorff-cover definition. The interval has dimension 1: interval length gives scale-1 contents at least 1, while subdivisions into intervals give zero q-measure for q>1. Hence dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. This covers n=0. With the upper bound the desired equality follows.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"x₀\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply to Euclidean Borel E and 0<s<D.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply to counting measure on I and summands ρ_i^s times the indicators of open J_i; these are nonnegative measurable functions.\\\"]}] }]}}\"}"}

